Commit message:
avoid eager loading through mixed re-exports (#11151)

With `strictExecutionOrder: true`, importing a local export from a
module that also re-exports pure values pulls the lazy chunk hosting
those values into startup. Initialization of such re-exports now belongs
to the consumer that imports them, so startup loads only what it uses.

```js
// shared.js
export * from './values.js'; // export const LAZY = 'lazy';
export const LOCAL = 'local';

// main.js
import { LOCAL } from './shared.js';
export const load = () => import('./lazy.js');

// lazy.js
import { LAZY } from './shared.js';
```

